        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ovary</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:41:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62196,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 83,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>They may be estrogenic, androgenic, or non-functioning.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:41:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62197,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 83,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>No data on epidemiology are available.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:41:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62198,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 83,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:41:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62199,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 83,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are usually wildtype for <em>DICER1</em> and <em>FOXL2</em>, with one tumour reported to harbour a <em>DICER1</em> mutation {24136150}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:41:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62200,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 83,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The appearance is variable; the tumours have a yellow or tan cut surface and are solid or solid and cystic. Haemorrhage and/or necrosis may be present.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:41:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62201,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 83,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histological features are variable, but distinctive features of a specific sex cord&ndash;stromal tumour are not identifiable. Changes seen in pregnancy include prominent oedema, luteinization, and prominent Leydig cells {6735262}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:41:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62202,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 83,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:41:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62203,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 83,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:41:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62204,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 83,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> immunohistochemical findings that support a diagnosis of sex cord&ndash;stromal tumour, but histopathological features of a specific tumour type are not present.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:41:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62205,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 83,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "<p>Malignant tumours are staged according to the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM classification (see <em>TNM staging of ovarian, fallopian tube, and primary peritoneal carcinoma</em>&nbsp;[[Brierley JD, Gospodarowicz MK, Wittekind C, editors. TNM classification of malignant tumours. 8th ed. Oxford (UK): Wiley-Blackwell; 2017.]]) and the FIGO staging system.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-15T11:20:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62206,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 83,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A few such tumours have been clinically malignant, with the reported 5-year survival rate being 92% {8651349}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:41:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]